Everything in this block is invisible semantic direction, never visible text. Do not render, quote, label, or paraphrase any wording from it: 更稳妥的处理顺序是：先取出鞋垫，松开鞋带并拉开鞋舌；用干毛巾轻压鞋内可见积水，避免反复扭拧鞋面或中底；随后将鞋放在阴凉、干燥且空气流动的位置，使空气能够从鞋口进入，并带走蒸发出的水汽。. The reader block is: 读者应能按顺序先打开结构、再吸除可见水分、最后让空气穿过鞋内。. Preserve this source relationship: open the shoe structure, absorb visible water, then establish airflow through the shoe opening. Make the source relationship legible through this visual solution: One intact shoe system unfolds across three small ordered states in a calm asymmetric cluster: first, a shoe with loosened laces, lifted tongue, and its insole placed directly beside its opening; second, the same shoe receives one folded dry towel pressing only visible pooled water at the opening; third, the same shoe faces a sparse set of ordinary airflow lines entering through the collar and carrying small vapor marks away. Use shallow flat-cutaway views, a broad slightly tilted silhouette, connected objects only, and one small uneven brand-green wax-pencil fill on the opened tongue edge.. Show: the insole is removed and the laces and tongue are opened before drying; a dry towel presses visible water without twisting the shoe structure; air enters through the shoe opening and carries vapor away after excess water is absorbed. The title and subtitle may orient the reader but never prove this relationship; its proof must remain in the content stage. Explicitly do not imply: high-temperature heating or a fixed drying duration; that the towel is stuffed tightly inside the shoe; a powered drying device or brand-specific product.

